==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|immer}} (also {{m|gmh|iemer}}, {{m|gmh|imer}}), from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|iomer|iomēr|always}}. From {{compound|io|mer|alt2=mēr||t1=always|t2=more|lang=goh|nocat=1}}. Cognate with Dutch {{m|nl|immer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɪmɐ/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-immer.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[always]]
# {{lb|de|with [[Appendix:Glossary#comparative|comparative]]}} [[more and more]]
#: ''Es wird '''immer''' kälter.'' — “It's getting colder and colder.
# {{lb|de|colloquial|unstressed}} {{non-gloss definition|used to emphasize another adverb of time, which itself is strongly stressed}}
#: ''Er kommt '''immer''' <u>nie</u> pünktlich.'' — “He’s never on time.”
#: ''Ich bin <u>oft</u> '''immer''' sehr vergesslich.'' — “I’m often very forgetful.”
#: ''<u>Manchmal</u> hab ich '''immer''' das Gefühl, dass...'' — “Sometimes I get the feeling that...”

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|immer gleich}}
* {{l|de|immer noch}}
* {{l|de|immer wieder}}
* {{l|de|immer wenn}}

===See also===
* {{l|de|ewig}}

